  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Agriculture obligated $517M in contracts in FY2027 to date. The Department of Agriculture recorded 3,415 awards so far in the fiscal year, with an average award size of $151K. Obligations fell 95.3% year over year. Fiscal history shows FY22 obligations were $10B, FY23 obligations were $11.5B, FY24 obligations were $11.6B, FY25 obligations were $9.6B, and FY26 obligations were $10.9B, while FY27 stands at $517M and is a partial fiscal year total. Contract activity in FY2027 to date is concentrated in resource and food-related industries. Logging leads NAICS categories at $99.6M, followed by Fruit and Vegetable Canning at $66.9M and Support Activities for Forestry at $42.5M. PEACHTREE LUMBER COMPANY, INC is the largest vendor at $99.6M, with PACIFIC COAST PRODUCERS next at $24.1M and ARCHER-DANIELS-MIDLAND COMPANY at $15.5M. Use this snapshot to prioritize outreach or proposal efforts where Agriculture is actively obligating funds during the current fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Department of Agriculture contract spending changed recently?",
        "body": "The Department of Agriculture obligated $517M in FY2027 to date, and that total is a partial fiscal year figure. Obligations fell 95.3% year over year. Fiscal year obligations were $10B in FY22, $11.5B in FY23, $11.6B in FY24, $9.6B in FY25, and $10.9B in FY26, showing a much lower FY27 to date total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are the largest product categories and top vendors in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "Logging is the largest NAICS category at $99.6M, followed by Fruit and Vegetable Canning at $66.9M and Support Activities for Forestry at $42.5M. PEACHTREE LUMBER COMPANY, INC is the top vendor at $99.6M, with PACIFIC COAST PRODUCERS at $24.1M and ARCHER-DANIELS-MIDLAND COMPANY at $15.5M. Other notable categories include Cheese Manufacturing at $38.7M and Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation at $29.9M."
      }
    ]
