  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Agriculture spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Agriculture obligated $517M in contracts in FY2027 to date. That figure is a partial fiscal year total. The Department of Agriculture recorded 3,415 awards in the period, with an average award size of $151K, and obligations fell 95.3% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Agriculture buy?",
      "a": "The Department of Agriculture is buying forestry, food processing, and related services in FY2027 to date. Logging accounts for $99.6M, Fruit and Vegetable Canning accounts for $66.9M, and Support Activities for Forestry account for $42.5M. Other purchases include Cheese Manufacturing at $38.7M and Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation at $29.9M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Agriculture's largest contractors?",
